===Etymology 2===
Probably a shortening of {{m|nl|jachtschip}}, from {{m|nl|jacht|t=hunt}} or {{m|nl|jachten||to hurry}} + {{m|nl|schip||ship}}. Ultimately from etymology 1.

====Noun====
{{nl-noun|n|-en|jachtje}}

# [[yacht]] {{gloss|fast, light and now often [[luxurious]] (sailing) [[boat]]}} {{defdate|from early 16th c.}}
#: {{syn|nl|jachtschip|jachtschuit}}
#: {{ux|nl|inline=1|Hij kocht een nieuw '''jacht''' voor zijn zomervakantie.|He bought a new '''yacht''' for his summer vacation.}}
#: {{ux|nl|inline=1|Ze vaarden op hun '''jacht''' naar het Caribisch gebied.|They sailed to the Caribbean on their '''yacht'''.}}
#: {{ux|nl|inline=1|Het kleine '''jachtje''' was snel en wendbaar.|The small '''yacht''' was fast and nimble.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Previously ''jacht'' could also take the feminine gender in this meaning, after etymology 1; this usage is obsolete.

